-What git is doing is read in one place, `Repo::stop()` in `src/operation.rs` (plan §2 #85): `Stop { operation, head }` with `Operation` (`Merge`, `SquashMerge`, `Rebase(Rebase)`, `CherryPick`, `Revert`, `Am`) and `Progress` (1 ≤ step ≤ total). Order as git's `wt_status_get_state`: `rebase-apply/` (`am` with `applying`), `rebase-merge/`, `MERGE_HEAD`, `CHERRY_PICK_HEAD`, `REVERT_HEAD`, the sequencer's first command, then `SQUASH_MSG`. Refs through `commit_named`, state files through one `rev-parse --git-path` call (`Repo::git_paths`), never a `.git/` path. `Stop::id()` is the stop without its progress (an `Am` keeps its patch number). `src/todo.rs` reads git's todo files (comments, first command, editor steps ahead). `tests/operations.rs` scripts every operation through `yamt_conflict_repo::operation_repo`.
+What git is doing is read in one place, `Repo::stop()` in `src/operation.rs` (plan §2 #85): `Stop { operation, head }` with `Operation` (`Merge`, `SquashMerge`, `Rebase(Rebase)`, `CherryPick`, `Revert`, `Am`) and `Progress` (1 ≤ step ≤ total). Order as git's `wt_status_get_state`: `rebase-apply/` (`am` with `applying`), `rebase-merge/`, `MERGE_HEAD`, `CHERRY_PICK_HEAD`, `REVERT_HEAD`, the sequencer's first command, then `SQUASH_MSG`. Refs through `commit_named`, state files through one `rev-parse --git-path` call (`Repo::git_paths`; `git_path` is its one-name case), never a `.git/` path; `read_if_present` and `exists` (missing = `None`/`false`, else `ReadFailed`) live in `src/repo.rs` for every git-dir file. A cherry-pick or revert has sequence progress only when the sequencer's first command is the same kind, the range makes commits (`opts` without `no-commit = true`) and `sequencer/head` names a commit. `Stop::id()` is the stop without its progress or editor steps ahead (an `Am` keeps its patch number); Continue, Abort and the moved-on check compare it. `src/todo.rs` reads git's todo files (comments, first command, editor steps ahead). `tests/operations.rs` scripts every operation through `yamt_conflict_repo::operation_repo`.
